OL,3,GNEWSAFormer council leader quits Reform
OL,4,AUK                                     
OL,6,FA former Reform UK council leader has  
OL,7,Fresigned from the party, citing        
OL,8,F"irreconcilable differences" with other
OL,9,Fmembers of the organisation.           
OL,11,FMartin Murray stepped down as leader of
OL,12,FStaffordshire County Council in        
OL,13,FOctober, the third Reform leader of the
OL,14,Fauthority to do so in the last year.   
OL,16,FIn a social media post, Murray said he 
OL,17,Fwould continue as an independent       
OL,18,Fcouncillor for his Cannock division,   
OL,19,Fbut added, "I have concluded that I can
OL,20,Fno longer, in all clear conscience,    
OL,21,Fremain a member of the Staffordshire   
OL,22,FReform Group."                         
